e_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.02942,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":19.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Septerna, Inc., a clinical-stage biotechnology company, discovers and develops G protein-coupled receptor (GPCR) oral small molecule products for the treatment of endocrinology, immunology and inflammation, and metabolic diseases. It develops PTH1R Program, oral small molecule Parathyroid Hormone 1 Receptor agonists for the treatment of hypoparathyroidism; SEP-631, an oral small molecule MRGPRX2 negative allosteric modulator (NAM) for chronic spontaneous urticaria and other mast cell diseases; and TSHR Program, an oral small molecule TSHR NAM for graves' disease and thyroid eye disease. In addition, it focuses on other therapeutic areas, including neurology, women's health, cardiovascular disease, and respiratory disease. It has global collaboration and license agreement with Novo Nordisk to discover, develop and commercialize multiple potential oral small molecule therapies for metabolic-related diseases based on certain specified molecular targets. The company was formerly known as GPCR NewCo, Inc. and changed its name to Septerna Inc. in June 2021. Septerna, Inc. was incorporated in 2019 and is headquartered in South San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Jeffrey T. Finer M.D., Ph.D. | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 123 people. Revenue per employee of $374K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers. Each employee generates $892K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $69K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Septerna, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $2.3B market cap on $46M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4175% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +7369.8pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -116% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $110M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 239 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -26.7% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 18% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Operating margins 149% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5529061102831595},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $73.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 29% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 320% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (SEPN) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/98/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_SEPN_Movement_102926020002_1793253602.html","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793253602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Septerna, Inc. (NASDAQ:SEPN) Stock Has Average Price Target of $52.44 According to Analysts","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/14/septerna-inc-nasdaqsepn-stock-has-average-price-target-of-52-44-acc